  "name": "KooKoo Singvögel — hourly birdsong clock",
  "description": "Twelve native German songbirds, one per hour. On each full hour the matching bird's recorded song plays. Reusable data manifest for embedding the clock in other apps.",
  "source": "KooKoo Singvögel (kookoo.eu) — illustrations & field recordings © KooKoo",
  "hourCycle": 12,
  "mapping": "sequential",
  "notes": "hour N (1..12) → bird N. 12:00 and 24:00 both play bird 12 (Pirol). Three audio tiers: chime (8s, mono, smallest — for embedders that just want a doorbell), short (33s, serves any cut up to 30s), full (the whole recording, 48s–300s). index.html fades in and out in software so it can cut anywhere with one curve, which is why no fade is baked into short/ or full/ — the 8s chimes do have one baked in.",
